  "name": "ok_turn_end_cancelled_by",
  "description": "turn/end.cancelledBy, the member that says *who* stopped a turn. It already existed in the contract (the recovery path writes `cli:recovery` and imported logs carry the old implementation's words); H2 gave the loop's own cancellation token a cause so the ordinary `POST /cancel` path can fill it in too. Free-form by design, as the second line shows: a reader must treat an unrecognised value as data, not as an error (AGENTS.md rule 2).",
